CounterStrikeExtended licensing scope
====================================

This repository is not licensed as a whole under MIT.

The MIT text in LICENSES/MIT.txt applies only to copyrightable original
contributions authored for this fork, to the extent their authors have the
necessary rights. For the initial development work, that scope is the original
build orchestration in CMakeLists.txt, CMakePresets.json, cmake/MSVCDefaults.cmake,
cmake/RuntimeTargets.cmake, hardware/CMakeLists.txt, tools/cmake_inventory.py,
tools/generate_runtime_sources.py, .gitignore, and original prose in this fork's
new docs and rewritten README.md. Original translation and MSBuild export tools
recovered from Git history retain that same original-contribution scope. It does
not cover quoted or copied third-party content.

Inherited source and modifications to it under src/, bundled libraries,
headers, artwork, provider interfaces, upstream-manifests.zip, and inherited build
selection data retain their existing notices, restrictions and unresolved
provenance. The cmake/targets/ files contain inherited source/flag/export
selections: maintaining them directly in CMake and generating inventories does
not grant new rights to the selected code or claim these inherited selections
are wholly MIT. The license of original build tooling provides no such grant.

No blanket MIT grant, commercial redistribution permission, or ownership of Valve,
Id, Steamworks, Miles, Aureal or other inherited content is asserted. See
docs/licensing.md for component evidence, retained notices and unresolved rights.
